$AB$ is a diameter of the circle, centre $O$. $CD$ is the tangent to the circle at $C$, and the tangent-chord angle between $CD$ and chord $CB$ is $65^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-2.4,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.543,1.839);
\coordinate (Rc) at (-0.547,2.675);
\draw (O) circle (2.4);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (C) -- (Rc);
\draw (A) -- (C) -- (B);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above left] at (C) {$C$};
\pic[draw, "$65^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=B--C--Rc};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find $\angle ABC$.
